{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a three-component radical 1,4-sulfonylacylation of 1,3-enynes using N-heterocyclic carbene (NHC) and visible light photoredox co-catalysis. The reaction couples acyl radicals (derived from aroyl fluorides via ketyl-type radicals) with allenyl radicals (generated from sulfonyl radical addition to 1,3-enynes) to produce tetrasubstituted allenyl ketones with high chemo- and regioselectivity.",
